{"kind":"report","text":"Completed checker-owned static preparation of exact I3 source 5d05de6f994d52b75a1e4f41ee9e41a8ffe646ac against ae3ea555eca36f767568a39920a34918d0982a46, under request 550a1bc5 and promise 46c92419. This is a finished preparatory report, with no ordinary source verdict, implementation acceptance or Git artifact owed.\n\nCoverage: five independent readers collectively covered all 110 current subjects, 1,605,287 bytes / 24,705 LF: 71 changed/new bodies FULL through EOF and 39 unchanged bodies transferred only from the same reader's verified personal FULL prior identities. All 84 native changes (43 modified, 28 added, 13 deleted) have complete additions/removals/context coverage; all 13 deleted prior bodies were read FULL (138,613 bytes / 2,867 LF), with exact deletion-body proofs including final-LF handling. Evidence.ts is one separately verified extra context, excluded from the 110 totals. Root read every contribution ledger/report fully, reconciled overlaps, independently matched all current metadata, verified all 128 reader rows' applicable prior identities/per-path deltas, all four aggregate deltas, architecture's 31 seals and prior reader seals. Zero unexplained mismatches. Collective whole coverage is not root personal whole-source coverage; root's exact whole and selected contexts are recorded separately. Final binding /tmp/artroom-checker-i3-5d05-preparation-binding.json, 48,833 bytes, SHA256 ae8eb4a93b11eef7d253607bddbd5ebace13e9149bb90543f0d7785114cf5279.\n\nP2 — Claim gateway lifecycle ownership across awaits. Gateway.ts309 checks open state before awaiting the valid push body at319; there is no new claim after that await. Two legitimate overlapping valid Gateway.forward calls can both pass, obtain plaintext334, mark/write forwarding342–346 and invoke upstream355. The fixed forwarded:1 record then hides two forwards. A host CAS may reject the second application: no two-applied-ref effect is claimed. The same ownership gap lets close/