retation stays with existing O11, not a duplicate finding. Root personally read current hold521–575/ledger241–308 and complete original evidence table3531–3549; independent derive/replay reader FULL covered all affected bodies. Production capability ports remain null; this is a component defect, not a demonstrated deployed outage or authority bypass.\n\nStill open: the three prior component P2s in finished report92fa170a (bounded parked startup prefix starvation; one-shot internal late-answer adapter loses an unavailable write without retaining/waking it, while its driver row is closed; common Evidence.body omission admitted where no owner validator narrows it). Current exact bytes and changed SQLite contexts do not repair them. M1 dependency finding514b35a9 remains separately owned: the plan still promises real six-scope founding before the complete pure whole Code behavior it requires. Landed Vitest serial grouping is test assembly/economy, distinct from this M1 rules dependency. Existing EH6–11/source-reader, pin identity, selected-read/replay, outcome kind, token-bound and cleanup/reservation decisions remain commissioned; no duplicate commission or invented stage fix.\n\nArchitecture: prepare reuses client transport, signed intent, serialized turn/seal/fold/fits, durable prepared identities and capability records. Pure rules, runtime ports, Git reader/gateway, operation driver and provider obligations remain separate. Git object type/size/hash and argv boundaries are meaningful; replay capability paths explicitly stop unsupported-definition and production NO_GRANT/capabilities:null/owners:null remain. New joint R1r15/R3r20 adoption is current design authority, not retroactive source credit. Proposed R1r16/R3r21/C2r7 are under separate ordinary reviews.\n\nSecurity: preserve signed intent, member/key/scope/grant checks, retained source attribution, authenticated own-answer and closed credential lifetime; the two findings must be resolved without weakening those rules. Gateway caller live-token claims and source-read authenticity remain trusted integration boundaries. No-final/no-destroy stays until coordinated C2/IA agreement. A closed gateway neither revokes a host token nor settles an unknown effect.\n\nSimplification: 13 obsolete files are actually removed with exact historical bodies and explicit remaining owners (parked log7→0, Git63→57, publisher7→1). Do not restore a policy layer or add another effect engine. Nonblocking: narrow derive README46's obsolete no-capability-rule wording; clarify lost-before/reached:1 reception label; refresh historical adoption status without backdating source acceptance. Ancestry repeated scans can later be indexed with a queue cursor under existing performance ownership, preserving latest-check selection, byte order and BFS order. Producer test/timing claims remain attributed, not independent validation; full cold install/edit/review economy and comparable10x remain unproved.\n\nComplete hosted/browser/device/provider/capacity/first-head/export/fork/snapshot/removal/product duties remain owed, including all five capacity dimensions and whole closure. No numerical test quota, fixed Jam gate or schedule-based scope reduction. Static immutable Git/text/provenance and built-in hashes/counts only. No tests, build, gate, install, typecheck, project imports/scripts, evaluator/protocol simulation/private diagnostics, provider/account/deployment action or source edit; all six private cloud-review script bodies stayed unopened.","body":{"finished":"true","head":"5d05de6f994d52b75a1e4f41ee9e41a8ffe646ac","no_git_artifact":"true"}}